From 9da2a61750eb52e01b30d9c926381fe77ac7af6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:20:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(xtask): sweep superseded test-harness units at the
 end of a gate run

One gate run builds one unit for each test target; camcraft-app has about
620 integration test binaries of about 100 MB each. Each change of the env
or of a dependency feature resolution gives every one of them a new unit
directory, and cargo never removes the old one, so each change added about
60 GB.

At the end of each run the gate now removes a test-harness unit
(test-lib, test-integration-test, test-bin) of its own target dir when this
run wrote a newer variant of the same target. Libraries and binaries stay.
The sweep does nothing while a cargo lock is held, another process uses the
tree's target dir, or CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off. A failed delete is a
warning. The summary prints the directories and GB removed.

Fixes #3169

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
