+#[test]
+fn the_gate_summary_runs_the_sweep() {
+    let src = include_str!("exec.rs");
+    let body = src.split("pub fn summary(").nth(1).unwrap_or_default();
+    assert!(body.contains("crate::unit_sweep::after_run(&self.root"), "the summary must run the sweep (#3169)");
+}

From 6e363d276492d8c68a361a737fbe4b077dc55876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:41:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(xtask): the unit sweep never follows a link and skips
 when unsure

Review of #3171:
- scan and delete check every level of the path with symlink_metadata and
  the Windows reparse-point attribute; a link is skipped, a linked target/
  or profile directory stops the sweep, and each unit is checked again just
  before its delete.
- The process check matches every form of <root>/target (as given,
  absolute, clean, canonical; case-folded on Windows). A form that cannot
  be resolved counts as live.
- after_run_with takes the env, so the off switch, the target-dir
  variables and the fallback start time are tested; a lock that cannot be
  probed and an unreadable process list are tested too.

Refs #3169

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
